<title>USA: Biocontrol glucose sensor 510(k) withdrawn.</title>
<headline>Biocontrol glucose sensor 510(k) withdrawn.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biocontrol Technology Inc said Thursday that the Food and Drug Administration is asking for another study before approving Diasensor 1000, the company's glucose sensor for diabetics.</p>
<p>The company said the FDA has withdrawn the company's 510(k) for the product so that it can be amended with data from an in-home study of the product that the FDA has asked for.  </p>
<p>The Diasensor 1000 is a nonintrusive devise that uses infrared light to measure blood sugar.</p>
<p>Biocontrol said it will respond to the FDA as soon as possible with an in-home study plan.</p>
<p>Biocontrol shares closed Wednesday at 1-15/16.</p>
</text>
